// Helper for issue-1353. Deliberately does NOT include value-source.cnx,
// so SHARED_LIMIT is genuinely undeclared here even though the entry pulls
// both files into the same run. Shared by BOTH include orders — see
// undeclared-value-sibling-source-first.test.cnx and its -consumer-first twin.
//
// The read below is at FILE SCOPE, while the negative control in
// declared-value-resolves.test.cnx reads its cross-file const INSIDE a
// function. The asymmetry is deliberate on both sides and must not be
// "tidied": a cross-file const in a file-scope initializer emits a
// non-constant initializer (#1218), so the control has to sit in a function
// body to fail only for the reason it exists to test. This file is
// test-error and therefore never compiles, so the file-scope form costs
// nothing here — and it is the form #1353 actually reported.
u32 borrowedLimit <- SHARED_LIMIT;

u32 valueConsumerFn() {
    return 1;
}
